# AGENT REFERENCE: ADMIN EXTENDED

Reviewed: 2026-08-24
Scope: `server/admin_extended` and direct dependencies
Purpose: behavior map for preserving the operator CSV user-import contract during repair or migration

## 0. Rules

1. Read `server/.agent-review` first, if it is added. No parent review existed at review time.
2. Treat `server/admin_extended`, its custom-admin registration, and persistence models as authoritative; use templates and examples as supporting evidence.
3. Preserve confirmed CSV and data contracts, not unreachable routing, partial imports, uncaught failures, or accidental security behavior.
4. Keep HTTP/admin transport, file parsing, row validation, import policy, persistence, and reporting separate.
5. Make authorization, atomicity, duplicate policy, file limits, row ordering, and failure reporting explicit.

## 1. Sources

- Primary: `server/admin_extended/forms.py`, `server/admin_extended/views.py`, `server/admin_extended/templates/upload.html`, `server/admin_extended/templates/success.html`, and `server/admin_extended/apps.py`
- Entrypoints: intended custom Django-admin paths `upload_csv/` and `download_example_csv/` declared by `core.admin.SystemAdmin.get_urls()`
- Dependencies: `server/core/admin.py`, `server/core/urls.py`, `server/templates/base.html`, `server/settings.py`, and `server/core/middleware/auth_middleware.py`
- Persistence: `server/peripheral_behavior/models/access.py`, `server/peripheral_behavior/models/menu.py`, and `server/peripheral_behavior/migrations/0001_initial.py`
- Runtime consumers: `server/event_contexts/device/lock_access_context.py`, `server/core/healthcheck.py`, terminal accounts, access permissions, and custom admin model registrations
- Evidence: static example CSV in `download_example_csv()`. No tests, docs, schema routes, or dedicated URL module cover this area.

## 2. Structure

| Path/component | Responsibility | Consumers |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `admin_extended.forms.CSVUploadForm` | Validate filename suffix, parse semicolon CSV, create users and access codes | `upload_csv_view` |
| `admin_extended.views.upload_csv_view` | Render upload form, invoke import, render all users on success | intended custom admin route |
| `admin_extended.views.download_example_csv` | Return fixed two-row example CSV attachment | upload template link; intended custom admin route |
| `admin_extended/templates/upload.html` | Show expected header, example-download link, multipart CSRF form, and validation errors | upload GET/invalid POST |
| `admin_extended/templates/success.html` | Show success text and every persisted game user | successful upload POST |
| `core.admin.SystemAdmin` | Declare admin-wrapped upload/download routes | currently no consumer because class is not registered |
| `peripheral_behavior.SkabenUser` | Persist unique game-user name and required description | access codes, terminal accounts, health bootstrap, admin |
| `peripheral_behavior.AccessCode` | Persist unique code owned by one game user | lock-event lookup, lock permissions, admin |

| Process/flow | Entrypoint/input | Runtime/output |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Upload page | Intended authenticated admin GET | `upload.html` with empty `CSVUploadForm` |
| CSV import | Intended authenticated admin multipart POST | Synchronous decode/parse and row-by-row ORM inserts, then `success.html` |
| Example download | Intended authenticated admin GET | `text/csv` attachment named `example.csv` |
| Access-code use | Device INFO containing `access_code` | Runtime lookup by exact stored code; importer itself emits no event or device update |

Current routing reality:

```text
/admin/ -> custom BaseSiteAdmin
  -> registered model-admin URL sets only
  -> SystemAdmin is never registered to a model
  -> upload_csv/ and download_example_csv/ are absent
```

`admin_extended` has no `urls.py`, and `core.urls` does not include these views directly. Therefore neither intended endpoint is reachable in current code. If upload rendering became reachable, its `{% url 'system:download_users_example_csv' %}` reference would still fail because no matching namespace or named URL exists.

## 3. Canonical Flows

### Intended CSV upload

```text
multipart POST with csv_file
  -> CSVUploadForm filename validation
  -> read entire file
  -> UTF-8 decode
  -> csv.DictReader(delimiter=";")
  -> for each row in source order
       -> require user_name, user_description, access_code keys
       -> require truthy values
       -> INSERT SkabenUser
       -> INSERT AccessCode linked to new user
  -> SELECT all SkabenUser rows
  -> render success page
```

This flow is implementation behavior only; routing defects prevent normal execution. Import has no transaction. Earlier rows remain committed when a later row fails. Within one row, user insert occurs before access-code insert, so access-code failure can leave an orphan user.

### Invalid upload

```text
missing file or filename not ending exactly in ".csv"
  -> form invalid
  -> render upload.html with field errors
```

Only field-cleaning failures participate in normal form error rendering. Header, row, decoding, and database errors occur inside `form.save()` after `is_valid()` and are uncaught by the view, producing an HTTP 500 instead of an invalid form response.

### Example download

```text
GET intended download route
  -> fixed ASCII/UTF-8 text
  -> Content-Type: text/csv
  -> Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="example.csv"
```

Body contract:

```text
user_name;user_description;access_code
John Doe;Awesome user;1234
Jane Smith;Cool user;6789
```

## 4. Contracts

### `CSVUploadForm`

- Role: accept one uploaded file and create one `SkabenUser` plus one `AccessCode` per parsed row.
- Input/state: multipart field `csv_file`; filename must end with lowercase `.csv`.
- Parsing: reads full upload into memory, decodes strictly as UTF-8, splits into lines, and uses Python `csv.DictReader` with semicolon delimiter.
- Required headers: exact, case-sensitive `user_name`, `user_description`, and `access_code`.
- Row behavior: extra columns are ignored; header order is irrelevant; values are not stripped or normalized; whitespace-only values pass truthiness validation; access codes remain strings, preserving leading zeroes.
- Output/effects: inserts rows synchronously in CSV order. Returns no import result, count, row diagnostics, or created-object collection.
- Invariants: every successfully completed row creates a new user and new code. Existing rows are never updated or reused.
- Edge cases: an empty file or header-only file imports zero rows and reports success. UTF-8 BOM can alter first header name. Case-insensitive extension, content type, encoding, size, row count, duplicate headers, numeric code format, and maximum field lengths are not validated by the form.

### Persistence models

- `SkabenUser.name`: unique, maximum 96 characters.
- `SkabenUser.description`: required, maximum 96 characters.
- `AccessCode.code`: unique, maximum 16 characters; model help text describes a numeric/card code, but model and importer accept arbitrary nonempty text.
- `AccessCode.user`: required foreign key with `CASCADE` on user deletion.
- `TerminalAccount.user`: also cascades on user deletion; import creates no terminal account.
- Access permissions point to codes and cascade when a code is deleted; import creates no permissions.
- Plain `model.save()` does not call `full_clean()`. Length and uniqueness failures therefore surface at database persistence rather than as form row validation.
- No custom save hooks, event publishing, or cache/device invalidation run for these two imported models.

### `upload_csv_view`

- Role: coordinate form binding and HTML rendering.
- GET/non-POST: creates empty form and renders `upload.html`.
- Valid POST: calls `form.save()`, queries all users without explicit ordering or pagination, and renders `success.html` directly.
- Invalid POST: renders `upload.html` with bound form and implicit HTTP 200.
- Output: no redirect-after-post. Browser refresh resubmits upload and normally reaches uniqueness failure.
- Failure behavior: catches no exception from decode, parse, validation in `save()`, or database writes.

### Admin routing and authorization

- `core.urls` mounts custom `BaseSiteAdmin` at `/admin/`.
- `SystemAdmin.get_urls()` declares relative `upload_csv/` and `download_example_csv/` paths and wraps both with `self.admin_site.admin_view()`.
- If registered, `admin_view()` would apply active-staff admin permission checks, CSRF protection where applicable, and admin-site behavior.
- Observed defect: `SystemAdmin` is never registered to any model, so `get_urls()` never contributes routes.
- Observed defect: both `path()` declarations omit URL names, while upload template reverses `system:download_users_example_csv`; no `system` URL namespace was found.
- Views themselves have no authentication/permission decorators. Routing them outside `admin_view()` would expose upload/download unless explicit protection is added.
- Project `AuthRequiredMiddleware` enforcement is commented out and provides no fallback protection.

### Templates

- `upload.html` extends global `base.html`, declares exact header text, uses multipart POST, includes CSRF token, and renders `form.as_p`.
- `success.html` extends global `base.html` and renders every user's name and description. Django autoescaping protects these values in normal template rendering.
- Template names are generic (`upload.html`, `success.html`) under app template discovery rather than namespaced as `admin_extended/...`; future apps can collide.
- `success.html` places a stylesheet `<link>` outside a template block after `{% extends %}`; inherited rendering may discard that markup. Global base already embeds its main generated stylesheet.

### App configuration

- `admin_extended` is installed in `INSTALLED_APPS`, so its templates are discoverable through `APP_DIRS=True`.
- `ServicesConfig` sets `name="admin_extended"` and `default_auto_field="django.db.models.BigAutoField"`.
- Package defines no models or migrations; auto-field setting currently has no persistence effect.

## 5. Failure Model

| Failure | Current outcome | Required outcome |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Operator opens intended upload/download path | Route not registered; 404/no reverse target | Register explicit, named, admin-protected routes and test resolved paths |
| Upload template renders after route repair | Reverse of `system:download_users_example_csv` fails | Use actual named URL and stable namespace |
| Filename lacks lowercase `.csv` | Bound form displays validation error | Preserve clear validation; decide case policy explicitly |
| Missing/invalid CSV headers | `forms.ValidationError` escapes `form.save()`; HTTP 500 | Validate before writes and attach file/row error to form response |
| Empty/header-only CSV | Success page with zero imported users | Define whether zero-row import is valid; report count |
| Invalid UTF-8/BOM | Decode/header exception; HTTP 500 | Detect supported encoding/BOM and return actionable validation error |
| Missing/empty later row | Earlier rows remain; exception becomes HTTP 500 | Validate all rows first, then atomic commit or explicit partial-import policy |
| Duplicate user name | Database integrity error; HTTP 500 | Define reject/update/skip policy with row number |
| Duplicate access code | New user may persist without code; database error becomes HTTP 500 | Atomic row/import and explicit duplicate policy |
| Field exceeds DB maximum | Database error after possible prior inserts | Validate model limits before transaction |
| Very large file/row count | Entire decoded content and all result users consume memory/time synchronously | Explicit byte/row limits, streaming or bounded parser, timeout policy |
| Database unavailable | Uncaught error and HTTP 500 | Atomic rollback plus operator-safe error and audit record |
| POST response refreshed | Same file resubmitted; uniqueness failure likely | Post/redirect/get with import result identifier |
| Unauthorized direct view exposure | Views have no local permission checks | Keep behind admin permission wrapper or enforce explicit staff permission |

- Concurrency/order: rows process sequentially per request, but concurrent uploads have no import lock or idempotency key. Unique constraints choose one winner; losing request can retain earlier rows or an orphan user. Success user ordering is database-dependent.
- Reliability: no `transaction.atomic()`, dry run, staging table, rollback report, idempotency, retry, audit record, or import status exists. Request lifetime owns entire operation.
- Security/operations: intended admin wrapper is not active because routes are absent. File validation trusts filename only; no explicit size/content limits exist in app. Imported text is autoescaped in HTML, but operator identity, source filename, checksum, counts, and failures are not logged.

## 6. Gaps

- Tests: no tests cover routing, admin authorization, form validation, parsing, persistence, rollback, duplicates, templates, downloads, or concurrency.
- Docs: no operational or development documentation references this import feature.
- Routing: intended public path is uncertain because model-admin URLs would be nested beneath a registered model path; no model registration or direct admin-site URL declares ownership.
- Validation: duplicate policy, blank/whitespace normalization, accepted encodings, BOM, numeric/code length rules, empty import, extra headers, row limits, and update semantics are undefined.
- Reporting: no created/skipped/failed count, row-number error, downloadable failure report, audit record, or persistent import identity exists.
- Defects: unreachable routes, nonexistent template URL name/namespace, uncaught post-validation errors, non-atomic partial writes, possible orphan users, zero-row success, unbounded all-user result, and no redirect-after-post.

## 7. Target Boundaries

| Target component | Responsibility | Constraints |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `AdminUserImportView` | Enforce staff permission, CSRF, request method, redirect, and result rendering | Stable named admin route; never call unprotected view directly |
| `CSVUploadValidator` | Validate file metadata, encoding, headers, row shape, normalization, and limits | No database writes; row-number diagnostics; preserve access codes as strings |
| `UserImportPolicy` | Decide duplicate/update/skip behavior and produce import commands | Explicit empty-file and whitespace policy; deterministic source order |
| `UserAccessRepository` | Atomically create/update users and codes | Respect unique names/codes, length limits, FK ownership, and rollback policy |
| `UserImportRecord` | Persist operator, source metadata, checksum, counts, timestamps, and outcome | Avoid storing raw sensitive file unless required and protected |
| `ExampleCSVResponse` | Serve versioned example matching accepted schema | Named protected route; semicolon and encoding contract explicit |

## 8. Migration Order

1. Characterize intended route/path, admin permission, example format, successful import, and every validation/persistence failure.
2. Register named admin-site routes and fix template reversal without changing import semantics.
3. Parse and validate the complete bounded input before any persistence side effect.
4. Define duplicate, normalization, empty-file, encoding, size, and partial/atomic import policies.
5. Extract import policy and repository; add atomic persistence and structured result/audit reporting.
6. Add post/redirect/get and remove direct row creation from the form after compatibility verification.

## 9. Minimum Tests

- Admin URL resolution, stable names/namespace, and template example link.
- Anonymous, authenticated non-staff, inactive staff, and active staff authorization.
- GET upload form, valid POST redirect/result, CSRF enforcement, and example download headers/body.
- Success with one/multiple rows, header reordering, quoted semicolon fields, Unicode, and leading-zero access code.
- Wrong extension, missing file, malformed/missing headers, missing data, whitespace, BOM, invalid UTF-8, empty/header-only input, extra columns, and oversized input.
- Duplicate user within file/database, duplicate code within file/database, length violations, and chosen update/skip policy.
- Dependency failure on user insert and code insert with verified rollback/partial policy.
- Concurrent duplicate uploads and idempotent retry/refresh behavior.
- Exact preservation of user/code relationships and no unintended permissions or terminal accounts.

## 10. Do-Not-Lose

- CSV logical fields: `user_name`, `user_description`, and `access_code`.
- Semicolon-delimited example and parser compatibility until operators receive a versioned replacement.
- Access codes stored as strings so leading zeroes and card identifiers survive import.
- One access-code owner relationship and existing unique user-name/code constraints.
- Active-staff authorization and CSRF protection intended by `admin_site.admin_view()`.
- Operator-visible validation errors and explicit success/failure counts in repaired flow.
- Existing downstream compatibility: imported users may own access codes and terminal accounts; imported codes may receive lock permissions and are looked up by exact value.

